\cf2 \cb3 Here are some common ways to use hooks:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa79\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Code formatting - Automatically format files after Claude edits them\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Testing - Run tests automatically when files are changed\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Access control - Block Claude from reading or editing specific files\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Code quality - Run linters or type checkers and provide feedback to Claude\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Logging - Track what files Claude accesses or modifies\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Validation - Check naming conventions or coding standards\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \
Here are some key practices for writing more secure hooks:\
1. Validate and sanitize inputs - Never trust input data blindly\
2. Always quote shell variables - Use "$VAR" not $VAR\
3. Block path traversal - Check for .. in file paths\
4. Use absolute paths - Specify full paths for scripts\
5. Skip sensitive files - Avoid . env , \'95git/ , keys, etc.\
\
We can have type change (in projects with typescript) or run test in Post Hook.\
We can use PreHook to inform if an existing file/code can be used instead of creating a new one.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa639\partightenfactor0
